menu "STARK"

    config STARK_DISPLAY_BAND_H
        int "Display render band height (lines)"
        default 40
        help
            Height of one DMA render band, in scanlines. Sizes the band buffer
            and the SPI2 max transfer (320 * STARK_DISPLAY_BAND_H * 2 bytes,
            default 25600, set by stark_board_init()). ARCHITECTURE.md §6.5, §9.

    config STARK_DISPLAY_SPI_HZ
        int "Display SPI clock (Hz)"
        default 40000000
        help
            SPI2 clock for the panel. 40 MHz is the target for the production
            PCB (ARCHITECTURE.md §9, HARDWARE.md §2.3). On a breadboard set
            20000000 (20 MHz): long jumper wires will not survive 40 MHz. The
            simulator runs at either.

    config STARK_DISPLAY_SWAP_XY
        bool "Swap X/Y (landscape)"
        default y
        help
            With the two mirror settings this selects the rotation. The
            defaults (swap only, no mirror: MADCTL MV, the usual ILI9341
            "rotation 1") give an upright 320x240 landscape image on a
            standard 2.8" module and on the simulated ILI9341, whose part is
            rotated 90 degrees in diagram.json for that reason. A mirror
            setting that does not match produces a transposed image, which no
            physical rotation of the panel can correct.

    config STARK_DISPLAY_MIRROR_X
        bool "Mirror X"
        default n

    config STARK_DISPLAY_MIRROR_Y
        bool "Mirror Y"
        default n

    config STARK_DISPLAY_BGR
        bool "Panel colour order is BGR"
        default y
        help
            If the red test bar shows up blue, this default is wrong for the
            panel: fix it here, never by swapping colours in stark_gfx.

    config STARK_DISPLAY_INVERT
        bool "Invert colours"
        default n

endmenu
